================================================================================
PART 2 — Apache License 2.0 (for the ArUco marker dictionary)
================================================================================

The ArUco marker generation features — specifically:

  • the JavaScript array `_ARUCO_CODES` (the 157-entry `QCMCAM_4X4_157h3`
    dictionary), located in `plan de classe.html`;
  • the bit-to-module decoding convention used to render those codes as 6×6
    matrices with the standard ArUco border,

are taken from QCMcam 2 by Sébastien COGEZ
— https://forge.apps.education.fr/qcmcam/qcmcam2 — whose repository is
published under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Full text: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

Summary of obligations for these components:

  • Attribution — the copyright notice and this reference must be retained.
    The credit "Sébastien COGEZ — QCMcam" is preserved in the application UI
    (QCMCam tab, ArUco marker print pages, About dialog) and must remain
    present in any redistribution.
  • Statement of changes — this file constitutes that notice: the dictionary
    is reproduced verbatim, and the rendering code is an independent
    reimplementation following the same convention, so that markers printed
    by this application are recognised by QCMcam's scanner.

NOTE — Until version 2.38.0, this application embedded the earlier 125-pattern
dictionary from `markers4x4.js` (qcmcam.net v1), distributed under
CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, and this section carried that license accordingly. That
mapping (`_ARUCO_N_TO_RAW` / `_ARUCO_OPTS`) has been REMOVED in 2.39.0 and
replaced by the dictionary described above.

The printable marker layout (`printSalleArucoMarkers`, `printArucoMarkersByList`,
`_buildArucoMarkerHTML`, and the associated `@media print` rules `#am-print`,
`.am-page`, `.am-tile`, etc.) is original work by this project's author and is
covered by Part 1 (MIT).

The rest of the application (placement, attendance, snapshots, tablets,
multi-room, AESH, etc.) remains under MIT License.

================================================================================
Why this dual licensing?
================================================================================

QCMcam is a free pedagogical tool distributed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. We
embed a local generator for its ArUco markers (so that teachers can print
only the markers they need for their salle, recto-verso, with our own
layout) — which makes the marker-generation code a derivative work of
QCMcam. Out of respect for Sébastien COGEZ's choice of license, we apply
CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 to those specific components, while keeping MIT for the
rest of the application to remain compatible with the broader open-source
ecosystem.

If you have questions or would like to use these components in a context
that is unclear under this licensing, please get in touch via the project
repository: https://github.com/Belenos-Toutatis/plan-de-classe
